; todo 52: conditional rewriting in a chain about free variables. Each line has its own names for
; its free variables (here `A`, `G`: "for all"), so the line before differed from the next one
; everywhere, not only at the place rewritten, and the instance of the conditional rule "below"
; (`get (ins c A G) n = get G n`, condition `n < c`) was not found -- unless it was written as a line
; of its own first. Found in proofs/classics/lambda-preservation.kurt ("ins-ins").
load numbers
const get, ins
arity get 2, ins 3
var A, G, B
real n, c

use n < c  ⇒  get (ins c A G) n = get G n                         "below"
use get (ins 0 B G) n = get G n                                    "front"

show n < 0 ∧ n < c  ⇒  get (ins 0 B (ins c A G)) n = get G n       "chain"
proof
    assume n < 0 ∧ n < c
        n < c
        get (ins 0 B (ins c A G)) n = get (ins c A G) n            ; front
                                    = get G n                      ; below
qed
